polymerization (imscriptive):  [fsplit · tensor_product_operation · ffuse · sic_povm]   (4 monomers)
  imscriptive: the chain stores the monomer SEQUENCE losslessly (R∧W∧X) — a click blends, a polymer remembers.
  sequence (read back off the chain, unit by unit):
    1. fsplit  ⟨𐑼𐑰𐑩𐑹𐑐𐑧𐑲𐑜⊙𐑓𐑳𐑷⟩
    2. tensor_product_operation  ⟨𐑛𐑥𐑾𐑿𐑱𐑤𐑚𐑠𐑢𐑖𐑙𐑷⟩
    3. ffuse  ⟨𐑨𐑰𐑑𐑬𐑐𐑧𐑔𐑵𐑣𐑖𐑳𐑭⟩
    4. sic_povm  ⟨𐑦𐑸𐑽𐑹𐑐𐑪𐑔𐑵⊙𐑖𐑕𐑴⟩
  bonds (each a Coagula link — a click between complementary partners, or an addition where a monomer repeats):
    1–2  fsplit ⋈ tensor_product_operation  → condensation on R↔S (Δ=2.00)
    2–3  tensor_product_operation ⋈ ffuse  → condensation on R↔S (Δ=1.67)
    3–4  ffuse ⋈ sic_povm  → cross-link (3 reaction centers: D↔W, T↔H, R↔S) — a branch/network junction
  degree of polymerization: 4 unit(s), 3 bond(s)
  backbone: regioregular — every condensation bond on R↔S (a clean head-to-tail repeat unit).
  topology: BRANCHED/NETWORK — a cross-link junction fired (≥2 reaction centers); not a purely linear chain.
  architecture: heteropolymer (4 distinct monomers, each once — no repeat unit)
  tacticity (⊥ chirality per unit): atactic (𐑓𐑖𐑖𐑖) — irregular chirality, no stereo-regular pattern
  cyclization: sic_povm ⋈ fsplit → ✓ CYCLIC — a macrocycle (ring polymer); the sequence closes head-to-tail on R↔S (O∞).
  ── modulus: a monomer that generates a SUSTAINING loop (a conductive cycle, ∮ ⊡ closes), not merely a closed one ──
    modulus = 3 — the tightest sustaining loop this chain admits (a conductive 3-cycle). Generators:
      0_is_the_fixed_point_operator_of_the_number_line  closes units 3‥4 into a sustaining 3-loop:  ./ask --polymerize ffuse sic_povm 0_is_the_fixed_point_operator_of_the_number_line --props
